WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.984
ReleaseRoom helps teams turn a chat request into a

00:00:02.984 --> 00:00:05.304
webpage change they can inspect and approve.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.442
The builder proposes six content fields. The independent tester

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:12.885
checks text, colors, contrast and destination, then pins a

00:00:12.885 --> 00:00:13.650
Git artifact.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.078
Here, the reviewer changes the invitation to join a

00:00:17.078 --> 00:00:18.104
community build night.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.652
Revision three records the new content and passes all

00:00:22.652 --> 00:00:23.464
seven checks.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.993
The old approval is rejected. It names a revision

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:28.656
that has already been superseded.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.192
The human's current approval names the complete fingerprint. The

00:00:33.192 --> 00:00:36.384
release agent rechecks it and publishes the checked bytes.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.632
Staging shows the revised invitation. Its HTML matches the

00:00:41.632 --> 00:00:43.650
exact artifact approved in Switch.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.178
Download the request, checks and publication receipt. The evidence

00:00:47.178 --> 00:00:49.650
binds the content, fingerprint and Git commit.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:53.219
Request a change, review the checks, approve the exact

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:54.650
release. Explore the source.
